Suggests: jotter
Description: Jupyter kernel for the Giac computer algebra system
 Runs Giac, the computer algebra system behind Xcas and the HP Prime, as a
 Jupyter kernel. Notebook front ends such as jotter, JupyterLab or VS Code
 can then evaluate Giac code in cells, with results shown as typeset LaTeX
 and 2D plots as SVG images.
 .
 The kernel is a small native program linked against libgiac. It needs
 neither Python nor a Jupyter installation; the kernelspec is installed as
 "giac". Help on a command (?factor), tab completion and interrupting a
 running computation are supported.
